THIRD-PARTY DATA

This repository redistributes data it did not author. The Apache-2.0 licence above
governs the code; it does not and cannot extend to the rows below. The machine-
readable register is THIRD-PARTY-DATA.json.

1. Virtual Metabolic Human (VMH) / Recon3D  --  MASTER_CROSSWALK.tsv

   Noronha A, et al. The Virtual Metabolic Human database: integrating human and
   gut microbiome metabolism with nutrition and disease. Nucleic Acids Research
   47(D1):D614-D624, 2019. doi:10.1093/nar/gky992
   Brunk E, et al. Recon3D enables a three-dimensional view of gene variation in
   human metabolism. Nature Biotechnology 36:272-281, 2018. doi:10.1038/nbt.4072
   https://www.vmh.life

   Eight of the twelve columns in MASTER_CROSSWALK.tsv are derived from a VMH
   Recon3D metabolite export: vmh, name, formula, inchiKey, hmdb, kegg, chebi,
   pubchem. The remaining four (seed, modeled_pathway, term_id, systems) are not.

   LICENCE STATUS: OPEN -- declared, not asserted. This project's own notes
   (working_map_nutrition/VMH_REFERENCE.md) record CC BY-NC 2.0 for Recon3D. The
   VMH database paper names no licence and says only that the data are "freely
   available". The operative terms have NOT been confirmed with the rights holder.

   Until they are, treat MASTER_CROSSWALK.tsv as NON-COMMERCIAL and as carrying a
   third-party attribution requirement, regardless of this repository's Apache-2.0
   licence. See MASTER_CROSSWALK.NOTICE.md.

2. US FDA food-substance inventories  --  FDA_ingredients/

   US Food and Drug Administration, retrieved 2026-08-02. Work of the US federal
   government (17 U.S.C. 105); public domain. No restriction on commercial use.

3. Open Food Facts  --  src/biology_as_code/data/fixtures/

   Open Food Facts contributors. https://world.openfoodfacts.org
   Data licensed under the Open Database License (ODbL) v1.0.

   67 meal fixtures declare `OpenFoodFacts (fallback macros)` in their own
   nutrition_provenance, supplying macro values where USDA FoodData Central had
   none. ODbL requires attribution in all cases and is SHARE-ALIKE for a publicly
   used derived database. Whether this fixture set is a derived database under
   ODbL, or a produced work using insubstantial extracts, is unresolved. The
   attribution above is required either way.

4. USDA FoodData Central  --  src/biology_as_code/data/

   US Department of Agriculture, Agricultural Research Service. FoodData Central
   (Branded, SR Legacy, Foundation). https://fdc.nal.usda.gov
   Work of the US federal government (17 U.S.C. 105); public domain. Attribution
   is courtesy. Not to be used to imply USDA endorsement.

5. MetaNetX/MNXref and ModelSEED  --  MASTER_CROSSWALK.xrefs.tsv

   Moretti S, et al. MetaNetX/MNXref: unified namespace for metabolites and
   biochemical reactions in the context of metabolic models. Nucleic Acids
   Research 49(D1):D570-D574, 2021. doi:10.1093/nar/gkaa992
   Seaver SMD, et al. The ModelSEED Biochemistry Database. Nucleic Acids Research
   49(D1):D575-D588, 2021. doi:10.1093/nar/gkaa746
   https://www.metanetx.org  ·  https://modelseed.org

   A sidecar to MASTER_CROSSWALK.tsv: one row per cell that VMH left OPEN and an
   independent source can fill. inchiKey and seed come from ModelSEED, chebi from
   ChEBI via MNXref, and the reconciliation between namespaces from MNXref itself.

   Both MNXref and ModelSEED are CC BY 4.0: commercial use is permitted and
   ATTRIBUTION IS REQUIRED. KEGG- and HMDB-derived cells are deliberately excluded
   because their terms do not permit what Apache-2.0 grants. See
   MASTER_CROSSWALK.xrefs.NOTICE.md.

Nothing else in this repository is third-party. See THIRD-PARTY-DATA.json for the
first-party list and the remedies available for item 1.

